s8-3-p28 : Block
s8-3-p28 = prose (cons "The two composites are identities by pair equality and function extensionality. Given an operation \(f\) on the pair representation, its operation on the sum-indexed representation is \(\mathsf{pack}\circ f\circ\mathsf{unpack}\). A dependent specification of \(f\), including its preservation proof, is transported along \(\mathsf{ua}(e_{m,n})\) in the corresponding family of operations and specifications. This is a complete index-level change; a byte layout or native in-place update adds its own state and address correspondence. In particular, packing the index family does not silently establish alias freedom or machine-layout equivalence." (cons "### 8.4 Executing an imperative operation is already a function" nil))
